WEBVTT

00:34.840 --> 00:36.850
There are so many of them!

00:37.350 --> 00:39.120
I can't just ignore them!

00:39.120 --> 00:41.460
But I don't have time to rescue everyone!

00:41.460 --> 00:43.400
What do I do?!

00:43.400 --> 00:47.070
The station... and Gojo-sensei... 
are just up ahead, too!

00:47.070 --> 00:48.140
Roe!

00:48.140 --> 00:49.360
That vocabulary!

00:50.830 --> 00:52.160
Inumaki-senpai!

00:52.160 --> 00:52.940
Salmon!

00:52.940 --> 00:53.770
Please help!

00:53.770 --> 00:55.000
Salmon, salmon.

01:03.950 --> 01:06.950
Episode 37
Red Scale

01:03.980 --> 01:05.430
Don't move!

01:17.510 --> 01:22.020
JUJUTSU KAISEN
Shibuya Incident

02:40.010 --> 02:42.510
22:10    Shibuya Station, Interior

02:49.520 --> 02:53.020
It Is Dangerous

03:05.530 --> 03:08.540
Tickets

03:08.540 --> 03:11.420
Automatic

03:30.680 --> 03:32.320
Yuji Itadori!

03:32.640 --> 03:34.320
My brothers' killer!

03:37.810 --> 03:38.820
Convergence!

03:37.820 --> 03:38.820
Convergence

03:40.300 --> 03:43.200
Blood Manipulation: "Convergence"

03:43.950 --> 03:48.450
is a skill that involves applying pressure 
to blood in order to compress it to its limit.

03:50.450 --> 03:52.920
The blood compressed with Convergence

03:52.920 --> 03:55.100
is then released through a single point.

03:55.100 --> 03:59.600
The initial speed of this blood 
enhanced with cursed energy

03:59.600 --> 04:01.560
well exceeds the speed 
of sound when released.

04:02.340 --> 04:06.430
This secret art of Blood 
Manipulation is called...

04:08.180 --> 04:09.430
Piercing Blood

04:08.180 --> 04:09.440
Piercing Blood.

04:23.240 --> 04:25.090
A double impact?

04:25.090 --> 04:26.770
What an odd technique.

04:42.740 --> 04:43.760
There's something

04:44.790 --> 04:46.780
I have to ask you.

04:47.760 --> 04:51.400
Did my little brothers leave 
behind any last words?

04:51.820 --> 04:52.890
Brothers?

04:52.890 --> 04:53.820
Tsk.

04:54.150 --> 04:57.150
I'm talking about the ones you two killed.

04:59.650 --> 05:01.830
No, not really.

05:03.150 --> 05:04.320
But...

05:06.710 --> 05:07.740
They were crying.

05:11.750 --> 05:12.740
Eso!

05:12.970 --> 05:14.170
Kechizu!

05:17.740 --> 05:19.090
Watch over me...

05:19.480 --> 05:25.010
This is your older brother!

06:42.810 --> 06:44.560
Shit...

06:45.540 --> 06:48.140
He got distance on me again.

06:48.620 --> 06:50.860
That beam of blood is too fast.

06:50.860 --> 06:52.640
I have a 50/50 chance to dodge.

06:52.640 --> 06:55.400
If my intuition is off and it hits my head...

06:55.890 --> 06:57.440
I'm dead.

06:59.990 --> 07:01.890
Then I should at least...

07:07.930 --> 07:11.910
determine when he fires it myself.

07:11.910 --> 07:14.100
He's luring me out.

07:14.100 --> 07:15.520
Fine, then.

07:35.430 --> 07:36.920
I knew it!

07:36.920 --> 07:39.730
That attack is only fast when first fired.

07:39.730 --> 07:41.950
Once I avoid it, I can lay on the pressure!

07:43.520 --> 07:45.190
Supernova.

07:44.690 --> 07:45.190
Supernova

08:17.130 --> 08:18.000
Tsk.

08:18.540 --> 08:20.090
I got hasty.

08:21.530 --> 08:23.870
It wasn't compressed enough.

08:26.140 --> 08:28.640
Shit! This bastard...

08:31.650 --> 08:32.970
is strong!

08:32.970 --> 08:33.960
Hey!

08:34.880 --> 08:37.650
Hey! What's the situation?

08:37.650 --> 08:39.800
Mechamaru! What have you been—

08:39.800 --> 08:40.660
Conserving energy.

08:40.660 --> 08:42.780
There's still a lot I need to do.

08:42.780 --> 08:45.380
Choso! Blood Manipulation, huh?

08:45.380 --> 08:46.180
You know about it?

08:46.180 --> 08:48.050
He's using the same 
cursed technique as Kamo.

08:49.740 --> 08:51.620
That thin-eyed third year, huh?

08:51.620 --> 08:52.900
Which means...

08:52.900 --> 08:54.600
I don't know its weakness.

08:54.600 --> 08:55.300
Geh!

08:55.300 --> 09:00.840
Blood Manipulation is treasured as one of 
the Kamo clan's hereditary techniques.

09:00.840 --> 09:04.250
The reason for that is "Convergence," 
which compresses blood with high pressure,

09:04.250 --> 09:08.040
plus "Piercing Blood" and "Blood Blade," 
which are derived from that,

09:08.040 --> 09:11.320
giving it a well-balanced response 
in close, mid, and long range.

09:11.780 --> 09:14.220
Since Choso won't bleed out, 
he has no openings.

09:14.220 --> 09:15.820
Thanks for the critical infor—

09:17.320 --> 09:20.660
I don't know its weakness, 
but I do have an idea.

09:20.660 --> 09:22.120
What is it?

09:22.120 --> 09:24.010
First, flee into the restroom.

09:24.010 --> 09:25.640
The restroom?! Why?!

09:25.640 --> 09:27.670
I'll explain later.

09:27.670 --> 09:29.930
There's maybe a 10% chance this works.

09:29.930 --> 09:32.680
Sorry, but if this fails, 
brace yourself for death.

09:32.680 --> 09:33.870
That's cruel.

09:33.870 --> 09:36.540
At this rate, you'll just get worn 
down until you're killed anyway.

09:45.730 --> 09:47.310
Idiot.

09:47.310 --> 09:50.480
That only leads to the 
restrooms and the elevator.

09:50.480 --> 09:53.490
No matter which you run to, 
you're trapped like a rat.

09:57.570 --> 09:59.020
What's that sound?

09:59.780 --> 10:02.380
This guy has beaten my brothers before.

10:02.380 --> 10:04.550
Those two wouldn't lose to some idiot.

10:04.960 --> 10:08.300
There's also that second voice 
that suddenly appeared.

10:09.520 --> 10:12.160
It would be right to assume 
he's planning something.

10:12.160 --> 10:13.310
Don't let your guard down.

10:13.310 --> 10:14.500
What's wrong?

10:14.500 --> 10:16.040
Not coming?

10:16.910 --> 10:19.000
You're a coward, huh?

10:19.000 --> 10:21.240
Just like your brothers.

10:22.310 --> 10:23.770
I'll kill you!

10:26.430 --> 10:29.020
JUJUTSU KAISEN

10:26.430 --> 10:29.020
JUJUTSU KAISEN

10:30.280 --> 10:32.400
You really are just like them.

10:36.480 --> 10:39.490
All three of you care 
so much for each other.

10:39.490 --> 10:41.610
It makes you easy to manipulate.

10:48.760 --> 10:50.830
It's all gone well so far.

10:50.830 --> 10:52.250
Now it's up to chance,

10:52.250 --> 10:53.540
Yuji Itadori!

11:05.830 --> 11:07.660
Too bad.

11:08.730 --> 11:11.190
That was your last chance.

11:11.190 --> 11:14.270
You're the one with nowhere to run now!

11:20.280 --> 11:22.600
Convergence dissolved?!

11:23.710 --> 11:27.330
In order to enhance the effects of 
the Blood Manipulation Technique,

11:27.330 --> 11:31.280
users constantly have the coagulation 
properties of their blood turned off.

11:31.960 --> 11:37.290
As a result, Choso's blood dissolves in 
water more easily than that of others.

11:37.570 --> 11:40.960
On top of that, once exposed to water,

11:40.960 --> 11:46.410
the osmotic pressure causes the red blood 
cells to expand and rupture their cell walls.

11:47.370 --> 11:53.840
This left him unable to control the blood 
cells that comprise 45% of his blood,

11:53.840 --> 11:56.310
breaking his Convergence.

11:57.160 --> 11:59.760
Mechamaru's aim was on the mark.

12:00.190 --> 12:02.160
In that situation,

12:02.160 --> 12:06.710
it was impossible for Choso to use 
Blood Manipulation outside his own body.

12:12.800 --> 12:16.770
Flowing Red Scale - Stack.

12:16.770 --> 12:19.580
Choso lacked combat experience,

12:19.580 --> 12:22.840
so he couldn't comprehend 
what was happening to him.

12:23.290 --> 12:25.460
He just coldly accepted the new reality

12:25.460 --> 12:28.880
and conducted his blood 
manipulation within his body.

12:30.210 --> 12:32.280
I don't understand the reasoning.

12:32.280 --> 12:35.040
There wasn't any opportunity for me to ask.

12:35.040 --> 12:37.860
But I do know one thing.

12:38.400 --> 12:40.620
I've dragged him into my turf!

13:49.300 --> 13:50.520
I can win!

13:52.390 --> 13:57.090
Choso had been keeping a clot of blood from being exposed and dissolving

13:57.090 --> 14:00.750
in the water as he strengthened 
said clot with cursed energy

14:00.750 --> 14:03.960
and compressed the 
coagulated lump to its limit,

14:05.820 --> 14:08.620
so the moment Yuji Itadori 
was convinced of victory,

14:08.620 --> 14:10.370
it pierced his liver.

14:11.320 --> 14:15.320
Blood Manipulation: Blood Meteorite.

14:15.320 --> 14:18.360
I screwed up! I assumed he couldn't 
use any more projectiles!

14:18.920 --> 14:21.040
What now? Where was I hit?

14:21.330 --> 14:24.320
This isn't the same as when 
I had a hole in my stomach!

14:24.320 --> 14:26.920
It destroyed something 
that shouldn't be broken!

14:27.340 --> 14:28.480
I'm going to lose...

14:29.000 --> 14:29.930
and die!

14:36.360 --> 14:39.850
I understand what my role is.

14:39.850 --> 14:42.680
Fushiguro, Kugisaki,

14:42.680 --> 14:46.200
the other upperclassmen, all of them

14:46.200 --> 14:49.620
will pass through here on 
their way to Gojo-sensei.

14:49.620 --> 14:53.120
So even if I die, I'm taking this guy out.

14:53.490 --> 14:58.080
I don't have to be the one 
to rescue Gojo-sensei.

14:59.280 --> 15:00.960
Three hits.

15:00.960 --> 15:03.110
A mere three hits,

15:03.110 --> 15:05.290
not counting the ones I guarded against.

15:05.760 --> 15:09.800
Those blows I took from Itadori 
dealt this much damage to me...

15:10.660 --> 15:12.790
Blood Meteorite's only 
strength is its hardness.

15:12.790 --> 15:15.600
It doesn't have the speed 
or impact of Piercing Blood.

15:15.600 --> 15:20.310
If I hadn't caught him by surprise, 
it wouldn't have been able to pierce him.

15:20.920 --> 15:23.170
Normally, Blood Manipulation sorcerers

15:23.170 --> 15:26.400
never coagulate blood like 
he did for Blood Meteorite.

15:26.400 --> 15:29.540
Even Blood Blade only 
solidifies the outline and

15:29.540 --> 15:33.240
circulates blood at high speeds 
to heighten its lethality.

15:33.240 --> 15:36.040
Even those sorcerers with 
Blood Manipulation can't

15:36.040 --> 15:39.080
extend their concentration 
to every blood vessel at once.

15:39.080 --> 15:41.880
So when they strongly coagulate their blood,

15:41.880 --> 15:46.090
it always poses the risk of 
causing spontaneous thrombosis.

15:46.490 --> 15:47.490
Bring it.

15:48.480 --> 15:55.850
However, Choso decided the risk 
posed by Yuji Itadori was far greater.

16:21.800 --> 16:22.410
He's strong!

16:32.360 --> 16:33.600
A tooth?!

16:37.230 --> 16:39.030
It was a feint?!

17:47.590 --> 17:48.590
Not yet!

17:52.090 --> 17:55.080
I haven't used my left fist since the start.

17:56.540 --> 17:59.350
He probably believes I can't use it anymore.

17:59.720 --> 18:02.810
So this attack using my 
right fist as a distraction

18:06.220 --> 18:07.390
will land!

18:11.450 --> 18:14.440
What was that response I felt?

18:30.750 --> 18:32.210
Too bad.

18:47.880 --> 18:50.830
He's still breathing.

19:00.990 --> 19:02.750
Apologize...

19:03.490 --> 19:06.010
to my brothers in the afterlife!

19:10.300 --> 19:12.270
How worthless.

19:12.270 --> 19:15.880
Losing to such riffraff.

20:02.330 --> 20:04.200
What?

20:10.060 --> 20:11.080
In that moment,

20:11.080 --> 20:13.940
memories flooded Choso's mind.

20:13.940 --> 20:16.940
Memories that didn't exist.

20:13.940 --> 20:17.020
Memories that didn't exist.

21:02.770 --> 21:03.760
Hey!

21:04.480 --> 21:05.990
You, too, Brother!

21:18.000 --> 21:21.410
What's happening? You're...

23:22.420 --> 23:23.320
There he is.

23:31.240 --> 23:33.600
He's alive, right?

23:33.600 --> 23:34.480
Yeah.

23:35.780 --> 23:38.320
Let's get this started, then.

23:40.840 --> 23:42.240
Moan-day?

23:42.240 --> 23:43.250
Monday.

23:43.250 --> 23:44.200
Tuesday!

23:44.200 --> 23:45.200
Mhmm!

23:45.200 --> 23:46.640
Weh-do-ness-day?

23:46.640 --> 23:47.330
Wednesday.

23:47.330 --> 23:48.680
Screw this!

23:48.680 --> 23:49.890
Next time, "Fluctuations."

23:48.780 --> 23:56.660
Next Episode
Fluctuations

23:49.890 --> 23:52.130
Who the hell came up with these readings?!

23:52.130 --> 23:54.620
Someone smarter than you, dummy.
